# Code owners of the Gladys repository.
#
# GitHub reads this file with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled on
# master: a pull request can only be merged once a member of an owning team
# of EVERY file it touches has approved it. The author of a pull request can
# never approve it.
#
# Review bots (cursor[bot], coderabbitai[bot]) are GitHub Apps, not members of
# these teams: their approval never satisfies this file. Keep it that way.
#
# Last matching pattern wins. The file is built in four layers:
#   1. everything belongs to the maintainers;
#   2. the areas open to the core team are listed explicitly;
#   3. inside those areas, the sensitive paths are closed again;
#   4. the release files are opened to the release team.
# A new directory is therefore maintainers-only until it is opened here.
#
# Teams are referenced by slug, and a team only counts as a code owner when it
# has explicit write access (or more) to this repository. The teams and the
# rules they enforce are described in MAINTAINERS.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Default: maintainers only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                                   @GladysAssistant/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Core team scope: fixes, devices and internal integrations
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
